# DDD: Package by Domain

Organize code by **domain (bounded context)**, not by technical layer.

- Each domain lives in its own package under `internal/<domain>/` and owns its entities, repository port, services, and adapters.
- Tests sit **next to** the code they test (`service.go` + `service_test.go`).
- No global layer folders like `services/`, `repositories/`, `models/`, or a central `tests/` full of unit tests.
- Use the ubiquitous language of the domain in names (`Membership`, `Segment`, `Estimate`), not generic ones (`Manager`, `Helper`, `Data`).
- Domains talk to each other only through exported ports/services, never through another domain's adapters.

```
✅ internal/segment/
     membership.go       membership_test.go
     repository.go       # port
     service.go          service_test.go
     adapter/memory/repository.go  repository_test.go

❌ internal/services/   (every service in one folder)
❌ tests/               (every unit test in one folder)
```
